{"slug": "sweet-potato-and-chickpea-curry", "nyt_id": 11649, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11649-sweet-potato-and-chickpea-curry", "name": "Sweet Potato and Chickpea Curry", "author": "Nigella Lawson", "description": "This is a warming rather than hot curry. You can taste the spices and enjoy their aromatic fullness. The ginger, chile and pepper flakes provide heat, while the coriander and cumin add a pleasurable earthiness. Meanwhile, the sweetness of the coconut milk, heightened by the soothing starchiness of the sweet potatoes, has as a counterpoint the fierce tang of tamarind. As a side dish, this recipe would be fine without the chickpeas, but as a meal, along with rice and maybe some steamed broccolini, they add heft and, if you're interested, protein.", "servings": {"text": "6 to 8 servings", "min": 6, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 50, "raw": {"total": "50 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 medium red onions, peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium red onions", "preparation": "peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 clove garlic, peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 bird's eye pepper, Thai chili or other very hot small pepper with its seeds", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "bird's eye pepper", "preparation": "Thai chili or other very hot small pepper with its seeds", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 2 ½- to-3-inch piece of ginger, peeled and cut into chunks", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "2 ½- to-3-inch piece of ginger", "preparation": "peeled and cut into chunks", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 tablespoons canola oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "canola oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ teaspoon hot red pepper flakes", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "hot red pepper flakes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ teaspoon ground ginger", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground ginger", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 teaspoon ground coriander", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground coriander", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 teaspoon ground cumin", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cumin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 ½ teaspoons ground turmeric", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground turmeric", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "3 cardamom pods, lightly crushed", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "cardamom pods", "preparation": "lightly crushed", "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "2 pounds (about 3 medium) orange-fleshed sweet potatoes, peeled and cut into ½- to-1-inch cubes", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "(about 3 medium) orange-fleshed sweet potatoes", "preparation": "peeled and cut into ½- to-1-inch cubes", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "1 ¾ cups coconut milk", "group": null, "quantity": 1.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "coconut milk", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "1 tablespoon tamarind paste", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "tamarind paste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "2 ¼ cups hot chicken or vegetable broth", "group": null, "quantity": 2.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "hot chicken or vegetable broth", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "4 to 5 cups (about 4 15 ½-ounce cans, drained) canned or cooked chickpeas (garbanzo beans)", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": 5.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "(about 4 15 ½-ounce cans", "preparation": "drained) canned or cooked chickpeas (garbanzo beans)", "optional": false}, {"position": 18, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped cilantro leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped cilantro leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 19, "raw": "Cooked white rice for serving (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "cooked white rice for serving", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 20, "raw": "Steamed broccolini for serving (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "steamed broccolini for serving", "preparation": null, "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a food processor, combine onions, garlic, hot pepper and ginger. Pulse until finely chopped. Place oil in a large saute pan over medium-low heat. Add chopped onion mixture and sauté until softened, about 5 minutes."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Add hot pepper flakes, ground ginger, ground coriander, cumin, turmeric, cardamom pods and ½ teaspoon salt. Stir to mix. Add sweet potatoes and stir until well covered in spices. Stir in the coconut milk."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Dissolve tamarind paste in hot broth and add to pan. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer, partially covered, until sweet potatoes are just tender, about 25 minutes. (Taste potatoes to be sure they are cooked all the way through, and allow additional cooking time if necessary.)"}, {"position": 4, "text": "Add chickpeas and simmer until heated through, about 5 minutes. Adjust salt to taste. Transfer to a warmed bowl and sprinkle with chopped cilantro. Serve, if desired, with white rice and broccolini."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 445.7, "protein_g": 12.6, "carbohydrates_g": 61.1, "fat_g": 18.6, "saturated_fat_g": 10.1, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 940.8, "fiber_g": 12.0, "sugar_g": 11.4, "unsaturated_fat_g": 7.2, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["gluten-free", "vegan", "vegetarian"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["chickpea", "fall", "one pot", "saute", "sweet potato", "winter"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/03/19/science/sweetpotatocurry/sweetpotatocurry-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 802}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2006-03-01", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:48:33.960480+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "sweet-potato-gnocchi-in-wild-mushroom-broth", "nyt_id": 5430, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/5430-sweet-potato-gnocchi-in-wild-mushroom-broth", "name": "Sweet-Potato Gnocchi In Wild Mushroom Broth", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "Four servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 90, "raw": {"total": "About 1 hour 30 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "3 ounces dried cepes", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "dried cepes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ½ pounds sweet potatoes", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "sweet potatoes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ cup all-purpose flour, sifted, plus up to ½ cup for kneading", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "all-purpose flour", "preparation": "sifted, plus up to ½ cup for kneading", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 tablespoons minced sage", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced sage", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "½ teaspoon salt", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 teaspoon freshly ground pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly ground pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "¼ cup grated Parmesan cheese", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "grated parmesan cheese", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Combine cepes and 6 cups water in a saucepan. Simmer over medium heat until reduced to 1 quart, about 30 minutes. Strain through a fine mesh sieve. Finely chop the mushrooms. Set both broth and mushrooms aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Preheat oven to 350 degrees. Place the sweet potatoes on a baking sheet. Bake until tender, about 40 minutes. Peel and pass through a ricer into a large bowl. Combine sweet-potato puree, flour, sage, salt and pepper. Place the dough on a lightly floured surface. Knead the dough, adding more flour if needed, until it is smooth and slightly sticky. Shape the dough into small dumplings. Set aside."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Pour the mushroom broth in a medium saucepan. Bring to a simmer over medium heat. Working in batches, drop the gnocchi into the broth. Cook 10 seconds after the dumplings rise to the surface, about 5 minutes total. Remove with a slotted spoon and divide among 4 warmed bowls. Ladle the broth over the gnocchi, sprinkle with Parmesan and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 316.9, "protein_g": 10.1, "carbohydrates_g": 65.3, "fat_g": 3.3, "saturated_fat_g": 1.8, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 6.3, "sodium_mg": 497.9, "fiber_g": 9.8, "sugar_g": 7.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 1.1, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["vegetarian"], "course": ["side dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["all-purpose flour", "bake", "mushroom", "soup", "sweet potato"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 61}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1993-01-31", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:43:49.153898+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "sweet-potato-salad-with-lime-pickle-and-cashews", "nyt_id": 12466, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12466-sweet-potato-salad-with-lime-pickle-and-cashews", "name": "Sweet Potato Salad With Lime Pickle and Cashews", "author": "Melissa Clark", "description": "Melissa Clark calls for homemade mayonnaise in this richly flavored yet light salad. It’s an easy task and well worth doing — but if working with raw eggs makes you squeamish, Hellmann’s or Duke’s are fine stand-ins. Lime pickle can be found in the South Asian food section of the supermarket. It is spicy, so use a light hand when adding it to the mayonnaise.", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "30 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ½ pounds sweet potatoes, peeled and diced into 1-inch pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "sweet potatoes", "preparation": "peeled and diced into 1-inch pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "6 tablespoons lime pickle mayonnaise", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "lime pickle mayonnaise", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 scallions, thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "scallions", "preparation": "thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped cilantro plus whole cilantro leaves for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped cilantro plus whole cilantro leaves for garnish", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ cup chopped roasted, salted cashews.", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped roasted", "preparation": "salted cashews", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Bring a pot of salted water to a boil. Add the sweet potatoes and cook until just tender, about 10 minutes. Drain and cool."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a large bowl, mix together the mayonnaise, scallions and cilantro. Add the sweet potatoes and cashews and gently stir to mix. Garnish with cilantro leaves and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 263.8, "protein_g": 4.0, "carbohydrates_g": 26.7, "fat_g": 16.3, "saturated_fat_g": 2.6, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 5.6, "sodium_mg": 339.3, "fiber_g": 4.0, "sugar_g": 5.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 13.2, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": [], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "cashew", "potato salad", "quick", "sweet potato", "winter"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2012/05/23/dining/23APPE2/23APPE2-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "Sweet potato salad with lime pickle and cashews.", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 189}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2012-05-23", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:56:54.801528+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "sweetbreads-with-morels-and-fava-bean-risotto", "nyt_id": 5425, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/5425-sweetbreads-with-morels-and-fava-bean-risotto", "name": "Sweetbreads With Morels And Fava Bean Risotto", "author": "Anthony Bourdain", "description": "Anthony Bourdain", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 75, "raw": {"total": "1 hour 15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 pounds sweetbreads", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "sweetbreads", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "¼ cup flour", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "4 ounces (1 stick) unsalted butter", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "(1 stick) unsalted butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 cups chicken stock", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chicken stock", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 tablespoons olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 onion, peeled and chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "onion", "preparation": "peeled and chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "8 ounces fresh morels", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "fresh morels", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 cup arborio rice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "arborio rice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "¼ cup finely grated Parmesan", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely grated parmesan", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "½ cup blanched and peeled fava beans", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "blanched and peeled fava beans", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "2 tablespoons pumpkin seed oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "pumpkin seed oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Soak sweetbreads for at least 8 hours (or overnight), changing water once or twice to remove blood. Put in a saucepan and cover with cold water, then place over medium-high heat to bring to a simmer. When moderately firm and opaque, remove from heat and transfer to ice water to stop cooking. Peel off as much membrane as possible, and remove any fat or gristle."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Heat oven to 225 degrees. Place flour in a large mixing bowl and season to taste with salt and pepper. Dredge sweetbreads in mixture and set aside. Place a large nonstick skillet over medium-low heat and melt butter. Add sweetbreads and sauté until golden brown and crispy on all sides. Remove from heat and transfer to a baking sheet; keep warm in oven."}, {"position": 3, "text": "In a small saucepan, heat chicken stock until just simmering. Place a medium saucepan over medium-low heat, and add olive oil. Add onion and sauté until translucent. Add morels and sauté until coated with oil, then add rice and sauté 1 more minute. Add ½ cup chicken stock and stir constantly until all liquid is absorbed. Repeat process using ½ cup of stock at a time, until rice is tender yet still firm; all stock may not be needed."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Add Parmesan and fava beans to rice, and stir gently to mix. To serve, place equal portions of sweetbreads and risotto on four serving plates. Drizzle pumpkin seed oil over risotto and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 1217.3, "protein_g": 43.4, "carbohydrates_g": 62.0, "fat_g": 88.4, "saturated_fat_g": 33.8, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 578.4, "sodium_mg": 1445.4, "fiber_g": 5.4, "sugar_g": 6.0, "unsaturated_fat_g": 46.9, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mediterranean"], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["arborio rice", "saute"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 22}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2003-06-11", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:43:46.669873+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "swiss-steak-with-mushrooms-and-red-wine", "nyt_id": 2424, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/2424-swiss-steak-with-mushrooms-and-red-wine", "name": "Swiss Steak With Mushrooms and Red Wine", "author": "Robert Farrar Capon", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "Makes 4 generous servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 140, "raw": {"total": "2 hours 20 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 thick chuck steak (about 4 pounds), bone in, or a 2- to 3-pound piece of round steak", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "thick chuck steak (about 4 pounds)", "preparation": "bone in, or a 2- to 3-pound piece of round steak", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 clove garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "Flour seasoned with salt and pepper (½ teaspoon salt and ¼ teaspoon pepper per half-cup of flour)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "flour seasoned with salt and pepper (½ teaspoon salt and ¼ teaspoon pepper per half-cup of flour)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "¼ cup olive oil or bacon fat", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "olive oil or bacon fat", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 large Spanish onion, chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large spanish onion", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 12-ounce package fresh mushrooms, sliced thick", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "12-ounce package fresh mushrooms", "preparation": "sliced thick", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup tomato puree", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "tomato puree", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "¼ cup Cognac", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "cognac", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 cup red wine", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "red wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 cup chicken (or other) stock", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chicken (or other) stock", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "½ teaspoon thyme", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "thyme", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "½ teaspoon savory", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "savory", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "½ teaspoon marjoram", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "marjoram", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "1 bay leaf", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "bay leaf", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "Salt and pepper as desired", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and pepper as desired", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Rub the steak all over with the garlic clove. Using a tenderizing mallet, the back edge of a cleaver or the edge of a heavy plate, pound into both sides of the steak as much of the seasoned flour as it will hold."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Heat the oil in a large skillet, brown the steak on both sides and remove to a suitable covered baking dish. Pre-heat oven to 300 degrees."}, {"position":